  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere of mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is divided into two unequal parts. The first part has a mass of <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and is converted into uniform disc of radius <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> . The second part is converted into a uniform solid sphere. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the moment of inertia of the disc about its axis and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the moment of inertia of the new sphere about its axis. The ratio <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is given by:",
    "image": null
  },
